{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>When a man takes</b> — in gematria: לא שיוקח (that she should not be taken)." "<b>ערות דבר</b> — rashei tevot: בעד שאין דבר שבערוה אלא בעדים (on behalf of — there is no matter of ervah except by witnesses)." "<b>דבר וכתב</b> — that speech is required together with the writing." "<b>And he writes for her</b> — לשמה (for her sake)." "<b>A scroll of cutting off</b> — three times in the Masorah in this matter, and the other (Isaiah 50:1) ספר כריתת אמכם. This is what they said: the scroll cuts off and nothing else cuts off. Therefore ספר כריתת is written three times — even though a woman is acquired in three ways, nothing else cuts off except the scroll."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:10:32.261410381Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}